@startuml "Strategy - Freight (Solution) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Four carriers, four ways of reaching a price

class ShippingDesk <<Context>> {
  - card : RateCard
  + book(shipment) : Quote
  + setCard(RateCard)
}

interface RateCard <<Strategy>> {
  + carrier() : String
  + quote(shipment) : Money
}

class ByDesi <<ConcreteStrategy>> {
  volume over 3000, billed as kilos
}
class ByWeightBand <<ConcreteStrategy>> {
  a printed table, one price per band
}
class ByZone <<ConcreteStrategy>> {
  route price + per kilo + fuel surcharge
}
class FlatRate <<ConcreteStrategy>> {
  one price, whatever it is
}

class CarrierBoard {
  + add(RateCard) : CarrierBoard
  + quoteAll(shipment) : List<Quote>
  + cheapestFor(shipment) : Quote
}

ShippingDesk o--> "card" RateCard
RateCard <|.. ByDesi
RateCard <|.. ByWeightBand
RateCard <|.. ByZone
RateCard <|.. FlatRate
CarrierBoard o--> "*" RateCard

note bottom of ByWeightBand
  <b>A lookup, not a rate.</b> One gram over a
  band edge costs a whole band more, which
  no Money perKilo() could express.
end note

note bottom of ByZone
  <b>The only card that holds moving state.</b>
  The fuel surcharge follows the oil price,
  not the contract.
end note

note left of CarrierBoard
  <b>Who chooses.</b> A carrier signed on Monday
  is a line here. No card and no desk is touched.
end note

@enduml
